  "_highlighterComment": [
    "Anna's real highlighter colours, used in the during-lecture instructions.",
    "These name physical objects, so they stay yellow/blue/pink in every pack --",
    "only their lightness shifts so they stay legible on a dark ground."
  ],
  "highlighters": {
    "yellow": {
      "light": "#806103",
      "dark": "#e8bf55"
    },
    "blue": {
      "light": "#2460cd",
      "dark": "#8fb4f7"
    },
    "pink": {
      "light": "#b72b71",
      "dark": "#f28fc0"
    }
  },
  "_laceComment": "`lace` is the colour the lace photograph is TINTED with at build time by tools/make_lace.py -- it is not a fill behind anything. White is not an option on the floral ground: the ground is near-white, so white lace disappears entirely.",
  "_patternComment": [
    "The floral pack paints a cream-and-blue ditsy floral on the page. It is built",
    "from radial gradients, not an SVG: an SVG data URI renders as an <img> but not",
    "as a CSS background-image or border-image on this machine, and it fails",
    "silently. Packs with transparent flower tokens paint nothing."
  ]
